{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Because the soul of the discerning person throughout the six days of creation is isolated in worldly pursuits, therefore on Sabbath it isolates itself to understand the work of HaShem and His wonders; therefore: 'For You have gladdened me, YHWH, in Your work.' This is like the Sabbatical year cycle, when they hear the entire Torah so that they may learn and fear. And the meaning: For You have gladdened me in my knowing all Your works, that they are upright."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 92, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:00.219704300Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}